Hoody patch rq-12230-revert.

What: undoes react-query 5.105.2 #12230 ("set the observer options before subscribing", issue #12227) in useBaseQuery
and useQueries, modern + legacy builds and src: observer.setOptions/setQueries run in an effect after
useSyncExternalStore subscribes again, as in 5.104.5. Nothing else in 5.105.x is touched.

Why: with #12230 the options effect runs before useSyncExternalStore's snapshot check, so a render that makes a new
observer result makes another render. Two Hub paths depend on the old order:
 1. A select that throws (core pageOf BAD_LIST, defineQuery reads): query-core 5.105.3 queryObserver.createResult sets
    `errorUpdatedAt = Date.now()` for a select error on every result it builds, so every render is a new snapshot and
    the page loops to "Maximum update depth exceeded" (PageBoundary). Guard: hub/src/core/query.selecterror.test.tsx.
 2. A held folder copy checked by two views at once (two panes on the same computer: each pane's HeldBand runs
    HeldTransfer -> useCopyCheck, files/changes.tsx; hash and tree reads staleTime 0): one view subscribed a render
    late and read files again that the other had just read (24-76 extra SHA-256 reads in a 172-read check, timing
    dependent). Guard: hub/src/pages/files/copycheck.bound.test.tsx "both panes' held bands share the fill".
What #12230 fixed and we give up again: a read whose key changed while its tree was hidden in <Activity>
(shell/pageHost.tsx keeps pages there) may fetch its old key once on reveal, one per such read (an agent/kit read
asks the old computer); a generation change makes the old queryFn throw before any request, and account/realm
changes remount the page (shell/switch.tsx). Hub ran this way on 5.104.5; no Hub code depends on the fix.
Drop this patch only when both guards pass without it: the copy check is shared by the views of one copy
and a throwing select no longer restamps its error time.

